<p>Errors are corrected in place and recorded here, newest first. To report one, see the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How corrections work</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Any reader may report an error through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>, giving the page, the sentence and the source that shows it is wrong. A report that is right is corrected on the page itself, so that no wrong statement stays up, and recorded here with the date, the page, what the page said and what it now says. A report that is not accepted receives a reply saying why, and if the point is one of reading rather than fact it may be published on <a href="/resources/objections/">Objections and replies</a> instead. Corrections made in the course of preparing the text, such as scanning errors in the printed sources, are logged in the same way. The log is kept newest first and is never pruned; a website that argues from the record of the gospels should keep a record of its own.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
